  "reference_solution": "SELECT s.sale_id,o.owner_id FROM sales s LEFT JOIN ownership o ON s.customer_id=o.customer_id AND s.sold_at>=o.valid_from AND (s.sold_at<o.valid_to OR o.valid_to IS NULL)",
  "solution_explanation": "Use a left temporal join with a half-open interval. The nonoverlap contract guarantees at most one match without hiding duplicate intervals via arbitrary ranking.",
  "hints": [
    "Ownership is a function of sale time.",
    "The shared handoff timestamp must belong to exactly one interval.",
    "Keep interval predicates in the left join and handle open-ended validity explicitly."
  ],
  "senior_review": "Validate interval nonoverlap and missing matches in production. That is a source invariant, not a license to silently discard sales.",
